{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Thoughts</b> — the words of the wicked — three joined [clauses]. And the interpretation: the righteous plan to do justice, and the wicked counsel to deceive them; and when they cannot, the wicked speak to ambush the blood of the righteous and kill them." "<b>And the mouth of the upright</b> — when they speak straightforwardly, their mouth will rescue them from those who lie in wait for them." "<b>Will overthrow</b> — the Name will overturn them from their place." "<b>And the house of the righteous</b> — those who plan justice, it will stand and not be overthrown."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads מחשבות as linking the surrounding clauses; 'three joined' refers to the three cola of the verse he sees as connected."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:19.437971575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}